B.Nb=s(["Apply a thick layer of organic mulch","Prune lower branches","Avoid overhead watering","Rotate crops annually"],t.s)
B.Oz=s(["Copper hydroxide sprays","Thick mulching","Compost tea foliar sprays"],t.s)
B.GX=new A.cx("Septoria Leaf Spot","Septoria lycopersici","Septoria leaf spot is a very common fungal disease producing numerous small brown spots with grey centers and dark borders on tomato foliage, starting from the lower leaves.",B.MR,B.NC,B.Nh,B.Nb,B.Oz,"Approximately 3 to 5 weeks for foliage regeneration.","Inspect lower leaves weekly. Pruning the lowest leaves as the plant grows prevents soil-dwelling spores from splashing up.",null)
B.Oc=s(["Tetranychus urticae mites","Hot and dry weather conditions","Dusty environments","Insecticide overuse killing natural predators"],t.s)
B.MW=s(["Fine yellow stippling on leaves","Dusty bronze or yellow leaves","Fine webbing on stems and undersides of leaves","Leaf drop"],t.s)
B.NI=s(["Apply abamectin or spiromesifen miticides","Spray leaves with high-pressure water to knock mites off"],t.s)
B.Oo=s(["Keep plants well-watered to reduce stress","Control dust on paths","Preserve natural predatory insects"],t.s)
B.Ne=s(["Insecticidal soaps","Neem oil sprays","Release predatory mites (Phytoseiulus persimilis)","Horticultural oils"],t.s)
B.H9=new A.cx("Spider Mites (Two-spotted Spider Mite)","Tetranychus urticae","Two-spotted spider mites are tiny arachnids that suck cell sap from tomato leaves, causing yellow stippling and fine webbing. They thrive and multiply exponentially in hot, dry weather.",B.Oc,B.MW,B.NI,B.Oo,B.Ne,"Approximately 2 to 3 weeks if mite population is suppressed early.","Inspect leaf undersides weekly for tiny moving dots during hot, dry spells. A magnifying glass helps detect early webbing.",null)
B.KT=s(["Corynespora cassiicola fungus","Warm and highly humid conditions","Leaves remaining wet for long periods"],t.s)
B.Ng=s(["Circular dark brown spots with concentric ring targets","Leaf yellowing","Dark pitted circular spots on fruit"],t.s)
