B.MO=s(["Insecticidal soaps","Neem oil or horticultural oils to suppress whiteflies","Yellow sticky traps"],t.s)
B.H8=new A.cx("Tomato Yellow Leaf Curl Virus","Tomato yellow leaf curl virus (TYLCV)","Tomato yellow leaf curl virus is a destructive virus transmitted by silverleaf whiteflies, causing severe stunting, leaf cupping, and yellowing. It severely limits fruit setting if infected early.",B.K7,B.K6,B.NP,B.Lq,B.MO,"Irreversible; infected plants do not recover and must be destroyed.","Monitor fields weekly for tiny whiteflies. Using yellow sticky cards helps catch vector activity early.",null)
B.LN=s(["Tomato mosaic virus (ToMV) or Tobacco mosaic virus (TMV)","Mechanical transmission via hands, clothing, or tools","Infected seed or planting material"],t.s)
B.LU=s(["Mottled light and dark green mosaic leaf patterns","Distorted fern-like leaf growth","Brown internal fruit rot (mosaic blemishes)"],t.s)
B.N5=s(["No chemical cure exists","Pull and burn infected plants immediately","Wash hands and tools in non-fat dry milk or disinfectant"],t.s)
B.Lc=s(["Use certified virus-free seed","Sanitize pruning tools between plants","Avoid smoking near tomato plants (TMV can survive in tobacco)"],t.s)
B.KX=s(["None; strict sanitation and immediate disposal are the only defenses"],t.s)
B.Ha=new A.cx("Tomato Mosaic Virus","Tomato mosaic virus (ToMV)","Mosaic virus is a highly stable, infectious virus causing mottled green-and-yellow mosaic patterns on tomato leaves and distorted fruit. It is easily spread by mechanical contact and contaminated tools.",B.LN,B.LU,B.N5,B.Lc,B.KX,"Irreversible; infected plants must be removed to protect the remaining crop.","Dip hands and tools in a dry milk solution weekly during pruning. Cleanliness is the only wall against mosaic virus.",null)
B.Ov=s(["Deep soil watering","Balanced calcium-rich nutrition","Consistent pruning","Proactive insect defense"],t.s)
B.LP=s(["Sturdy deep green leaves","No spotting or margins yellowing","Fuzzy healthy trichomes","Balanced growth"],t.s)
B.Kc=s(["Prune suckers to maintain single-leader or two-leader systems","Continue watering base of plant","Apply calcium amendments"],t.s)
B.MB=s(["Inspect weekly","Follow strict crop rotation","Add organic compost to soil"],t.s)
B.OB=s(["Mulch with organic straw","Feed with fish emulsion","Weekly foliar sprays of compost tea"],t.s)
B.GY=new A.cx("Healthy Tomato Leaf","Solanum lycopersicum","A healthy tomato leaf is compound, deep green, and slightly fuzzy, optimizing gas exchange and sunlight absorption to feed ripening tomatoes.",B.Ov,B.LP,B.Kc,B.MB,B.OB,"N/A","Pinch out small suckers in leaf axils weekly to focus plant energy on main stems and fruit development.",null)
